Z||000000||TONY_C||11-16-2001||02:13 PM||||Does anyone know what would cause the speedo in a 91 accord to work sporadically.  Any help would be greatly appreciated.  TIA.<p>[This message has been edited by TONY_C (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||11-16-2001||06:32 PM||||Does it have an electric or cable driven speedo?  If it's cable driven, it could be that the cable needs replaced, or the speedometer head is getting worn out (highly unlikely the speedo is worn out in a honda).  If it's an electric speedo, the speed sensor may need replacement.  It's probably on the transmission somewhere.<P>Do you have a service manual for the car?  Service manuals are invaluable if you do your own repairs, and will save you enough to pay for themselves the first time you fix it on your own instead of taking it to a shop.  For that car you can get a book at the Autozone for pretty cheap, I'm sure they have it on the shelf.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
